n we all wake up  on november the 4th there are so many  questions that need answering  and my first guest is literally the  perfect person  to talk us through them all joining me  now is the legend  the one and only dan rather he is the  president  of news and guts media and co-author of  the book  what unites us reflections on patriotism  i am  so happy to talk to you this evening in  the midst of what  feels like living history so let's start  off with just your broad view  on the state of the race what's your  reaction been to  the closing messages we've seen from the  joe biden campaign  versus the donald trump campaign with  just one day to go  well first of all in the great arc of  history  we always argue that every presidential  race is important  but this does figure to be one of the  more consequential  presidential campaigns certainly of the  modern presidential era  that's number one number two as we go  through the last hours before the last  day  of voting to my surprise  uh president trump wants to go out on  the line he's going to fire  dr fauci uh that seems a a strange go  out line to me but  he chose that line i think he did so  because he understands that the  overriding narrative of the campaign  so far has been the virus has been  coronavirus  and joe biden and the democrats have  made that their number one theme  president trump likes to play offense  not defense but he's had to play such  fierce defense against that uh that he  invokes the firing of dr fauci  uh the best thing donald trump has going  for him  is there was some uh good economic news  a little earlier in the week  and i do think that gave him at least  some movement some momentum  but he's not emphasizing the economic  message he's going down saying you fire  found you so we shall see  i do think it's important to take a deep  breath you know  uh having covered this i covered my  first presidential campaign on the air  in 1952 if you can believe that  so much has changed but y